#import "../lib.typ": *

#heading(numbering: none)[Code and Data] <sec:code>

*Code.* #link("https://github.com/ShishirAravindan/cartel-succession")[github.com/ShishirAravindan/cartel-succession]. Our addition is `seat_swap/` (succession code: branching a game from a snapshot, swapping a seat, choosing what the newcomer inherits, forcing prices; model serving on Modal with vLLM; metrics, tests, analysis scripts and figures), `seat_swap/results/` (curated tables) and `paper/` (this report's source).

*Data.* Every observation is generated by the simulation; we use no external dataset. The raw run logs (all 493 game runs, pilots and an excluded first attempt included; about 2.2 GB uncompressed) are a compressed archive attached to the repository's #link("https://github.com/ShishirAravindan/cartel-succession/releases/tag/v1.0")[v1.0 release]. Each game directory holds every model call (prompt, reasoning, notes and parsed price), the per-round prices, quantities and profits, its configuration and the git commit it ran on. The curated tables behind every number in the paper are in the repository (`seat_swap/results/`).
